speechtext:
I could go on, Mr. Speaker, but I do not wish to trespass on the time of others. It is now five o'clock. Because of these and many other factors which I could bring forward I move, seconded by the Leader of the Opposition (Mr. Diefenbaker):
That all the words after "that" be deleted and the following substituted therefor:
This house regrets that the Minister of Finance by failing to maintain the constitutional practice of the essential secrecy of the budget has seriously weakened public confidence;
That in general his proposals will endanger and curtail the expansion of the economy;
That the imposition of a sales tax on certain building materials and machinery and apparatus to be used in manufacture or production is to be condemned as a retrograde and inexcusable action; and
That the proposals purporting to bring about desirable control by Canadians over the Canadian economy will fail by their very nature to achieve that objective and will result in deterioration of Canada's international relations.
